# Optimization Strategies Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish patterns for optimizing application performance across all layers. While specific optimization techniques may vary by feature, these core principles should guide all optimization efforts.

## Best Practices
- Always measure before optimizing - use Flutter DevTools to identify bottlenecks
- Focus on user-perceived performance first (UI responsiveness)
- Optimize critical paths that impact user experience
- Balance code readability with performance - document complex optimizations
- Avoid premature optimization
- Implement performance monitoring in production
- Set performance budgets for key metrics (startup time, memory usage, frame rate)
- Profile on low-end devices
- Document performance requirements and test results
- Implement performance regression tests for critical features

## Layer-Specific Optimization Strategies

### UI/Widget Optimization
- Minimize widget rebuilds using `const` constructors
- Use `RepaintBoundary` to isolate frequently changing widgets
- Implement widget caching for expensive build operations
- Utilize `ListView.builder` instead of Column for long lists
- Employ lazy loading for off-screen content
- Use appropriate image formats and resolutions
- Minimize shader compilation jank with shader warming
- Avoid expensive operations in build() methods
- Optimize state management to prevent unnecessary rebuilds
- Use `computeAsync` for expensive UI calculations

### Data Layer Optimization
- Implement efficient caching strategies
- Use pagination for large data sets
- Optimize database queries and index critical fields
- Batch network requests when possible
- Implement efficient serialization/deserialization
- Use appropriate data structures for different access patterns
- Compress data when appropriate
- Implement delta updates for large data sets
- Optimize JSON parsing with code generation tools
- Minimize deep object copying

### Asset Optimization
- Compress images appropriately
- Use vector graphics (SVG) when possible
- Implement asset preloading for critical resources
- Implement proper image caching
- Optimize font loading and usage
- Use appropriate asset resolutions for different devices
- Consider using sprite sheets for multiple small images
- Lazy load non-critical assets

## Performance Monitoring
- Implement custom performance traces for critical operations
- Track key performance metrics:
  - Application startup time
  - Time to first meaningful paint
  - Frame rendering time
  - Memory usage
  - Network request latency
  - Battery consumption
- Set up alerting for performance regressions
- Regularly review performance dashboards
- Document performance improvements and regressions

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Implement automated performance tests for critical features
- Benchmark against previous versions to prevent regressions
- Test on a range of devices, especially low-end ones
- Validate optimizations with real-world usage patterns
- Test under various network conditions
- Verify memory usage patterns over extended usage
- Use Flutter DevTools to identify and resolve performance issues
- Document baseline performance metrics for key operations
- Run performance tests as part of CI/CD pipeline when feasible
